<title>HONG KONG: HK Oct retail sales up seven pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Oct retail sales up seven pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong October retail sales totalled a provisional HK$19.1 billion, up seven percent on the year and up three percent on the month in value, Census and Statistics Department figures showed.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets:</p>
<p>						     Oct	Sept</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on-year)  - value   +7	 +7</p>
<p>					 - volume  +2	 +3</p>
<p>			  (on-month) - value   +3	 -3</p>
<p>					 - volume  +2	 -4</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on-year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +7	 +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  -2	 -4</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   -2	 +5</p>
<p>					 - volume  -3	 +3</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value   +6	 +7</p>
<p>					 - volume  +6	 +6</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   +4	 +9</p>
<p>					 - volume  -3	 +4</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value  +11	 +2</p>
<p>					 - volume  +4	 -3</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value   -4	 -8</p>
<p>					 - volume  -9	-13</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value  +26	+22</p>
<p>					 - volume +25	+21</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value   +3	 +8</p>
<p>					 - volume  +3	 +8</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
